!!! oculus/window/operations.mat
!!! Window management operations: create, focus, raise, minimize,
!!! maximize, close.
!!!
!!! Each operation is idempotent and returns the updated window.
!!! Operations on an already-closed window are no-ops.

book oculus.window.operations

read everything from ny.lang.core
read everything from oculus.window.geometry
read everything from oculus.window.lifecycle
read everything from oculus.window.record
read everything from oculus.window.workspace

!!! Create a new window at the given position with the given label.
public create-window receives position-x as override long, position-y as override long, width as override long, height as override long, label as text, window-id as override long returns window begin paragraph
    value origin is build point with x being position-x, y being position-y
    value geom is build rectangle with origin being origin, width being width, height being height
    value ws is build workspace with index being 0, label being "workspace-0"
    give build window with identity being window-id, state being window-state.Created, geometry being geom, workspace being ws, z-index being 0, focused being false, label being label
end paragraph

!!! Set a window as the focused window (returns true if successful).
public focus-window receives window-obj as window, should-focus as boolean returns window begin paragraph
    value updated is build window with identity being window-obj.identity, state being window-obj.state, geometry being window-obj.geometry, workspace being window-obj.workspace, z-index being window-obj.z-index, focused being should-focus, label being window-obj.label
    give updated
end paragraph

!!! Raise a window to the top of the z-order.
public raise-window receives window-obj as window, new-z-index as override long returns window begin paragraph
    value updated is build window with identity being window-obj.identity, state being window-obj.state, geometry being window-obj.geometry, workspace being window-obj.workspace, z-index being new-z-index, focused being window-obj.focused, label being window-obj.label
    give updated
end paragraph

!!! Minimize a window (only if it's visible).
public minimize-window receives window-obj as window returns window begin paragraph
    value updated is build window with identity being window-obj.identity, state being window-state.Minimized, geometry being window-obj.geometry, workspace being window-obj.workspace, z-index being window-obj.z-index, focused being false, label being window-obj.label
    give updated
end paragraph

!!! Close a window.
public close-window receives window-obj as window returns window begin paragraph
    value updated is build window with identity being window-obj.identity, state being window-state.Closed, geometry being window-obj.geometry, workspace being window-obj.workspace, z-index being window-obj.z-index, focused being false, label being window-obj.label
    give updated
end paragraph
